#
# EVERY CHECKOUT GETS THE BYTES THE REPOSITORY HOLDS, ON EVERY MACHINE (#512).
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites each text
# file's LF to CRLF on checkout. Under Cygwin that breaks every script before
# its first line runs (`$'\r': command not found`), and it breaks the images
# too, without a word: the build context is the checkout (`COPY . ./`), so
# each entrypoint, postgres/'s scripts and build-typescript.sh would reach a
# Linux container with a CR on every line, and a `#!/bin/bash\r` names an
# interpreter that does not exist.
#
# NO CONVERSION RATHER THAN `eol=lf`, because not every file here is LF: the
# XACML conformance suite under xacml/conformance/ is upstream's, byte for
# byte, and CRLF there. Normalising it would change files nobody edited, and
# the test vectors elsewhere are compared byte for byte too. `-text` turns
# conversion off in both directions whatever a person's autocrlf says, so a
# Windows checkout is the same bytes as a Linux one. tests/tools/
# host-platform.sh has the rest of what Cygwin needs.
* -text
